description:
Build the core of a PE viewer like PE-bear or `dumpbin`: load a 64-bit PE file from its bytes, list its sections, find which section an RVA belongs to, and list every import.

```cpp
struct Section { std::string name; std::uint32_t virtualAddress, virtualSize, rawPointer, rawSize, characteristics; };
struct Import { std::string dll; std::string function; std::uint16_t ordinal; };

class PeFile
{
public:
    bool load(std::vector<std::uint8_t> bytes);
    std::uint32_t entryPoint() const;
    std::uint64_t imageBase() const;
    const std::vector<Section>& sections() const;
    std::optional<std::uint32_t> rvaToOffset(std::uint32_t rva) const;
    std::string sectionOf(std::uint32_t rva) const;
    std::string permissions(const Section& s) const;
    std::vector<Import> imports() const;
};
```

- **load** keeps the bytes and reads the headers as in lesson 1.03; it returns false (and the object holds nothing) for anything that is not a valid 64-bit PE.
- **rvaToOffset** as in the practice; **sectionOf** names the section containing an RVA, or returns `""`.
- **permissions** gives three characters for a section: `r` or `-`, `w` or `-`, `x` or `-` (read 0x40000000, write 0x80000000, execute 0x20000000).
- **imports** reads the import directory (data directory 1, whose RVA is at offset 120 of the optional header): one descriptor of 20 bytes per DLL, until an all-zero one. For each, read the DLL name, then the 8-byte thunks of its import name table (`OriginalFirstThunk`, or `FirstThunk` when that is 0) until a zero thunk. A thunk with the top bit set is an import by ordinal (`function` empty, `ordinal` the low 16 bits); otherwise it is the RVA of a 2-byte hint and the name (`ordinal` 0). Imports are listed in file order. Any RVA that cannot be turned into a file offset stops the reading cleanly, returning what was read so far.

